# SkySpy vLLM — best config from the DGX Spark tuning run (2026-07-24).
# Winner by blended reward (0.6 quality / 0.4 speed): Qwen2.5-32B-AWQ = 0.665.
# Ranking (baseline knobs, screen): 32B-AWQ 0.665 > 7B 0.630 > 30B-A3B 0.593 > 14B 0.589.
#
# Highest eval quality (0.875, 14/16) with mid-pack speed; the 0.6 quality weight
# makes it beat the faster-but-weaker 30B-A3B MoE. Stage-B knob tuning was cut
# short (1 trial) to end the prod outage — the Optuna study is checkpointed and
# resumable for finer knob search in a maintenance window.
#
# Drop into .env, then: docker compose --profile gpu up -d vllm
VLLM_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen2.5-32B-Instruct-AWQ
VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=32768
VLLM_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.80
VLLM_MAX_NUM_SEQS=64
VLLM_MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=8192
VLLM_KV_CACHE_DTYPE=auto
VLLM_TOOL_PARSER=hermes
VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS=--enable-prefix-caching --enable-chunked-prefill --quantization awq
# DGX Spark note: on the GB10 the vLLM container also needs VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM=0
# (DeepGemm FP8 MoE kernel asserts on Blackwell) and gpu-util <= 0.85 (128 GB is
# unified with the system). Both are baked into tuning/vllm/ launch defaults.
